[h1]Spire Mentor: beta[/h1]

[b]Beta build of Spire Mentor, for testing.[/b] Unsubscribe from the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3821016481]regular Spire Mentor item[/url] while this one is installed: the game loads only one mod per id. Everything the regular item does, this one does too; its page has the full description, keys and settings.

[h2]New in this beta (0.11.6-beta.1)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Linux[/b]: the AI now runs on native Linux Steam too (x86-64, glibc 2.28 or newer: any current distribution). Please report how it goes; it has not been played on Linux much yet.
[*][b]A new AI program[/b]: the coach (SimAdvisor) is rewritten as one native program instead of a bundled Python one. It should advise exactly as before; tell us if anything differs.
[*][b]Instinct plays all five characters[/b]: Ironclad, Silent, Defect, Regent and Necrobinder, on v0.111.0 and v0.113.0, with new weights.
[*][b]The Fool gets combat advice[/b] on v0.113.0: fights are searched and ranked as for the other characters. Map, card reward, shop, rest and event screens get no advice for The Fool yet (no trained network for it).
[*][b]More of v0.113.0 simulated[/b]: the Wuppy relic (its pet, Wuppy's Loyalty and the Restore rest option) and the Punch Off event's fight.
[*][b]Panels beside the game[/b]: when the panels' window is closed, a button next to the badge brings it back, so you no longer have to find it under Panels.
[*][b]Workbench[/b]: The Fool's art and every character's energy orb show in the replay of a live run, and live runs replay on the game build they were played on.
[*][b]Fixes[/b]: a game set to another language (Chinese, for example) no longer has fights refused for orb, monster or potion names. Enchant screens tell the AI which enchantment the pick gets. Watch the AI play with Instinct keeps the character you picked.
[/list]
Everything else is the regular item's 0.11.5.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Windows or Linux.[/b] The AI runs as a bundled program (SimAdvisor). On a Mac the mod loads but the coach cannot start. On Linux the panels' own window also needs python3 with PyGObject, GTK 3 and WebKitGTK (webkit2gtk-4.1) installed, and the game on X11 or XWayland (its default); without them the panels stay in the game.
[*][b]Game builds v0.111.1 (stable) and v0.113.0 (public beta), including hotfixes of them such as v0.113.1.[/b] A game update can break the mod until a new version is out.
[*][b]BaseLib[/b] (by Alchyr), which Steam installs alongside this mod as a required item.
[/list]

[h2]Reporting a bug[/h2]
Press [b]Ctrl+Shift+B[/b] (or [b]Panels → Report a bug[/b]) the moment something goes wrong, say what happened in one line, and press [b]Send report[/b]. Nothing is sent until you press Send. Paste the link it puts on your clipboard into a comment here or a GitHub issue.

